<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pereslavl-Zalessky</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pereslavl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pereslavl-Zalessky is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslavl">Yaroslavl</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-pleshcheyevo">Lake Pleshcheyevo</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky">Yuri Dolgoruky</a> in 1152 and named after Pereyaslavl in the south, it was the seat of an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> principality and the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1302 and is one of the Golden Ring towns, with its white-stone Transfiguration Cathedral of 1152–1157.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pereslavl-zalessky.jpg" alt="Pereslavl-Zalessky" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Игорь Шелапутин · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F-%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%89%D0%B0%D0%B4%D1%8C-%D1%88%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD-2019-0450.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
